        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How fast should a beginner run on a treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Slow enough to talk in short sentences. For many beginners that is somewhere around 4 to 5.5 mph, roughly a 15- to 11-minute mile, with walking breaks at about 3 to 3.5 mph. Those are typical ranges rather than targets: shorter, older or heavier beginners are often nearer the bottom, and the talk test matters more than the number.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How long does it take to be able to run 30 minutes on a treadmill?",
