          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It is optional. The 1% convention comes from research showing it matches the energy cost of outdoor running at faster speeds, where air resistance matters. At beginner speeds the difference is small, so 0% or 1% are both fine. Avoid raising the incline further while you are learning to run, because it adds load to the calves and Achilles tendons.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How many days a week should a beginner run on a treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Three running days a week on non-consecutive days is a common and sensible starting point. Bones and tendons adapt more slowly than heart and lungs, and the rest day between runs gives them time. If you want to use the treadmill more often, walk on the days in between rather than adding extra runs.",
